<concept id="t00267">
	<title>Hybrid Electric Vehicle (HEV) system</title>
	<prolog>
		<metadata>
			<keywords>
				<indexterm>HEV (hybrid electric vehicle) system</indexterm>
			</keywords>
		</metadata>
	</prolog>
	<conbody>
		<p>The Kia Hybrid Electric Vehicle (HEV) combines a gasoline engine and an electric motor for power. The electric motor uses a high voltage Hybrid Electric Vehicle (HEV) battery.</p>
		<p>Depending on the driving conditions, the HEV computer selectively operates between the engine and the electric motor, or both at the same time.</p>
		<p>Driving the vehicle with the electric motor (powered by the HEV battery) increases fuel efficiency.</p>
		<p>The engine occasionally turns on (even when the vehicle is idling) to act as a generator to maintain the charge level of the HEV battery. The battery power also charges when you are slowing down or using regenerative braking.</p>
